(a) The city clerk shall be designated as the records management officer whose duties shall consist of the following:
(1) Establishing and maintaining an active and continuing program for the economical and effective management of records;
(2) Creating and implementing procedures and regulations for efficient and effective records management;
(3) Assisting each department in the implementation of a program of records management;
(4) Conducting training in records management to designees of departments;
(5) Preserving records of continuing value;
(6) Removing records not in common and current use from office space to city storage facilities and removing other records upon the expiration of their day to day utility in the office in accordance with approved disposition standards;
(7) Systematically eliminating all other records in accordance with approved disposition standards; and
(8) Serving as the open records officer, pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 50-18-71(b)(1)(B) of the Georgia Open Records Act, and accordingly responding to requests under the Georgia Open Records Act, O.C.G.A. § 50-18-70, et seq.
(b) The assistant to the city clerk shall be designated as the assistant open records officer and perform the duties of the open records officer, in the event of the city clerk's absence or unavailability.
(c) All requests under the Georgia Open Records Act, O.C.G.A. § 50-18-70, et seq., shall be submitted to the open records officer and/or assistant open records officer as designated in this section.
(Ord. No. 2006-24, § 1, 8-7-06; Ord. No. 2016-03, § 1, 2-1-16)

