The city shall accept private inspection services only if such services are provided by a registered professional engineer in conformance with and as authorized by O.C.G.A. § 8-2-26(g). Any such engineer shall be prequalified by the city in accordance with the provisions of O.C.G.A Section 8-2-26(g)(7) and this section. The qualifications of an engineer shall be evaluated by the city building inspector on the basis of the engineer's expertise with respect to the objectives of the inspection, as demonstrated by the following factors:
(1) Experience: The engineer shall have at least five (5) years experience as a certified professional engineer and five (5) years of appropriate Southern Building Code Congress International, Inc. (SBCCI) certification.
(2) Education: The engineer shall have at least the following level of education:
a. At least a bachelor's degree from an Association of Bachelor of Engineering and Technology and Technicians (ABETT) accredited college in one of the following areas, as appropriate for the inspection to the conducted: acoustical engineering, composite engineering, civil engineering, engineering science and mechanics, electrical engineering, materials science and engineering, or mechanical engineering;
b. A current Georgia professional engineer registration; and
c. A current company registration with the Secretary of State, Corporations Division, to practice consulting engineering.
(3) Training: The engineer shall have at least the following SBCCI certification(s), as appropriate for the inspection(s) to be conducted:
a. Housing rehabilitation code enforcement officer or housing rehabilitation inspector;
b. Zoning and property standards inspector;
c. Residential electrical inspector;
d. Building inspector, building plan examiner or chief building code analyst;
e. Commercial electrical inspector;
f. Plumbing inspector, plumbing plan examiner or chief plumber code analyst;
g. Mechanical inspector, mechanical plan inspector or chief mechanical code analyst;
h. One-and two-family dwelling inspector;
i. Fire inspector I, fire inspector II, fire safety plan examiner or chief fire prevention code analyst;
j. Electrical inspector, electrical planner examiner or chief electrical code analyst;
k. Commercial combination inspector;
l. Legal and management (examination);
m. Coastal construction inspector.
(Ord. No. 2002-28, § 1, 7-1-02)
